        <briefdescription>
<para>Snapshot the high-precision clock into a timestamp struct. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Three volatile reads, no branching, no function call overhead. Safe to call from ISR context (provided the overflow ISR has a higher priority — see <ref refid="syn__port__hpclock_8h" kindref="compound">syn_port_hpclock.h</ref>).</para>
<para>Compiler barriers between the MSB (SRAM) and LSB (peripheral bus) reads prevent the compiler from reordering the accesses.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ts</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An <ref refid="structSYN__HPTimestamp" kindref="compound">SYN_HPTimestamp</ref> lvalue (not a pointer). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
